  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Neutral distancing with sein and haben",
     "texto": [
      "In the press and in formal statements, the writer uses **sei** (singular) and **seien** (plural) to attribute statements to a source without committing to their accuracy. The verb **sein** is the only one in German that keeps distinctive forms in all persons of Konjunktiv I (**ich sei, er sei, wir seien, sie seien**).",
      "With **haben**, the third person singular form is **er/sie habe**. In the plural, since **sie haben** matches the indicative, the substitute form **hätten** (Konjunktiv II) is used to keep the indirect style marker."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Subject",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "sein (Konjunktiv I)",
       "lengua": "estudio"
      },
      {
       "texto": "haben (Konjunktiv I / II)",
       "lengua": "estudio"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Example",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "er / sie (sg.)",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "sei",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "habe",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Der Sprecher sagt, er sei bereit und habe Zeit.",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "sie (pl.)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
